 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**No. The Aussie is strong against the yen right now, not weak.**\n\n- **Latest:** A$1 buys about **¥109.67** (RBA 4pm rate, 16 October 2026).\n- **Versus a year ago:** End-October 2025 was ¥100.84, so the Aussie is up about 9%.\n- **Versus early 2023:** January 2023 was ¥91.69, so it's up about 20%.\n- **Recent high:** About ¥114.5 to ¥114.6 in late August and early September 2026. It has since slipped about 4%.\n\nThe move is mostly the yen weakening, since the Aussie is buying more yen than it did before. If you're asking because you're travelling to Japan or buying Japanese goods, your dollar goes further than it has in a long time.",
